Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Servicii de inginerie
Overview 
 We are looking for an experienced Java Full-Stack Developers to join our team in Bucharest and contribute to the design, evolution, and delivery of mission-critical Air Traffic Management (ATM) systems. You will be involved across the full software lifecycle, from architectural decisions and technical design to implementation, testing, and production integration. This is a hybrid role, requiring 3 days per week on-site at the client's office in Bucharest. 
 Responsibilities 
Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain new functionalities, while customizing and improving existing ATM software components and modules;
Take ownership of technical, technological, and methodological choices aligned with the selected software architecture, ensuring adherence to code quality, security standards, reuse policies, and product roadmaps;
Author clear technical design and justification files in compliance with project quality standards;
Maintain and optimize CI/CD pipelines from design to delivery, ensuring reliable, production-ready software releases;
Bring up-to-date knowledge of modern software engineering practices while anticipating future platform developments.
 Requirements 
Proven experience in software engineering across backend and frontend development;
Strong proficiency in Java and hands-on experience with the Spring Boot framework;
Solid working knowledge of TypeScript;
Experience with Git, CI/CD tools (Jenkins, GitLab CI), and configuration/change management tools (Jira);
In-depth knowledge of Agile, Scrum, and SAFe methodologies;
Strong software testing practices, technical documentation skills, analytical and conceptual thinking, self-reliance, and clear communication;
Full professional fluency and proficiency in English.
 Nice to Have 
Prior experience with Gradle;
Domain familiarity with Air Traffic Control (ATC) or Air Traffic Management;
Knowledge of aeronautical software and hardware assurance standards (e.g., EUROCAE ED-109 / RTCA DO-278) and requirements analysis.
 What We Offer 
Opportunities to grow through involvement in complex international projects;
A collaborative environment with knowledge-sharing initiatives and technical communities;
Meal vouchers as part of your monthly benefits;
Private medical insurance, supporting your health and wellbeing;
25 days of annual paid leave under a full-time employment contract;
Flexible working arrangements, aligned with project requirements and client environments;
Access to technical training programs and professional development resources.
 Ready to embed yourself in the future? Let’s partner with us to power what’s next! 
 Please note that only suitable candidates will be contacted and that by applying to this role you are being informed about your personal data being processed by Avel Technologies. 
 You can find more details here: https://aveltechnologies.com/privacy-policy/
